  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mapping of the book and publishing sector in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The mapping of the book and publishing sector in Africa aims to enable the 54 African Member States to UNESCO to be better equipped to respond to the challenges and priority development needs of the book and publishing sector in their countries. It will also allow UNESCO to elaborate a roadmap to support the development of this strategic sector in Africa through relevant programmes. The mapping is carried out through an in-depth consultation process with Governments and publishing professionals in order to collect data and information on the state of the book and publishing sector in their country. As a result, in addition to mappings at country level for each country, the mapping report will also include an analysis of the trends, challenges and growth opportunities of the book and publishing sector throughout the African continent.</narrative>
  </description>
